    "description": "Write a part as one MIDI item: starts at start_beat (quarter notes from the\nproject start; beat 0 = bar 1), lasts length_beats * repeat. replace: first\ndelete the track's items that overlap that span, so writing a part again\nrewrites it instead of stacking on it.\nnotes: \"PITCH@BEAT[:LENGTH[:VELOCITY]]\" separated by spaces, BEAT relative to the\nitem start; PITCH as 0-127 or a name (C4 = 60, F1, Bb0); chords as \"F1+C2@0:2\".\nDefault length 1 beat, velocity 100. repeat: play the pattern that many times,\nevery length_beats. Example, a bar of 8ths: \"F1@0:0.5:120 F1@0.5:0.5:90 Ab1@1:1\".",
    "input_schema": {
      "properties": {
        "channel": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Channel",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "length_beats": {
          "title": "Length Beats",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "notes": {
          "title": "Notes",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "repeat": {
          "default": 1,
          "title": "Repeat",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "replace": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Replace",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "start_beat": {
          "title": "Start Beat",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "track_index": {
          "title": "Track Index",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "track_index",
        "start_beat",
        "length_beats",
        "notes"
      ],
      "title": "write_notesArguments",
      "type": "object"
    }
  }
